+# Graceful candidate unload
+
+The concurrency trial's explicit clean-shutdown constraint exposed that both
+recipe unload paths used `docker rm -f` on running candidates. They now request
+`docker stop --timeout -1` by verified immutable container ID, wait at most
+60 seconds in the Anvil client, and perform plain removal only after success.
+A stop failure or client deadline prevents removal and shared-memory cleanup;
+Docker receives no automatic SIGKILL deadline. A concurrent restart is rejected
+by non-forced removal. The cache remains intact.
+
+Docker documents the negative timeout behavior at
+<https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker/container/stop/>, observed 2026-09-09.
+The focused model, discovery, and graceful-unload suite passed 159 tests.
